 34AR c  {+32}S+2p|){+34}Ar from J|p=0+ {+32}S ground state.                    
 34AR c  1986Al15: a 25.4-MeV {+3}He beam was produced from the time-of-flight  
 34AR2c  facility at the University of Colorado. The target was natural sulfur  
 34AR3c  evaporated onto a 2-mg/cm{+2} gold foil. Neutrons were detected using  
 34AR4c  three NE224 liquid scintillators with FWHM=350 keV. Measured           
 34AR5c  |s(E{-n},|q). Deduced levels, L-transfers, J, and |p from local,       
 34AR6c  zero-range DWUCK-DWBA analysis. Comparisons with shell model and analog
 34AR7c  states in {+34}S.                                                      
 34AR c  1972Bb01: 14-MeV {+3}He beam from the 7 MV Van de Graaff accelerator at
 34AR2c  Frankfurt University impinged on natural {+32}S targets. Measured      
 34AR3c  |s(E{-n},|q). Deduced ground state, J, and |p from zero-range          
 34AR4c  DWUCK-DWBA analysis.                                                   
 34AR c  1968Ha09: 4.5-6.2-MeV {+3}He beams from the de Graaff accelerator at   
 34AR2c  Hahn-Meitner-Institut fur Kernforschung Berlin and impinged on FeS     
 34AR3c  targets. Measured neutron spectra using a time-of-flight spectrometer. 
 34AR4c  Deduced 5 levels.                                                      
 34AR c  1967Mi02: 10-12-MeV {+3}He beams from the ONR-CIT tandem accelerator   
 34AR2c  impinged on natural sulfur targets. Neutron energies were measured by  
 34AR3c  means of (n,|a) reactions induced by neutrons in the active volume of a
 34AR4c  silicon semiconductor detector. Deduced Q value and one level.         
 34AR c  1967Mc03: 4.9-5.6-MeV {+3}He beams from the SUNI 6 MeV Van de Graaff   
 34AR2c  accelerator at Southern Universities Nuclear Institute, South Africa   
 34AR3c  impinged on natural CdS targets. Neutrons were detected using a NE213  
 34AR4c  liquid scintillator. Measured |s(E{-n},|q) and deduced g.s. and 2      
 34AR5c  levels.                                                                
 34AR c  1984Be05: 4.6-6.5 MeV {+3}He beams from the University of Kentucky Van 
 34AR2c  de Graaff Accelerator impinged on CdS and ZnS targets. Neutron angular 
 34AR3c  distributions and excitation curves were measured with a neutron       
 34AR4c  time-of-flight facility.                                               
